# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Everything listed here would otherwise be uploaded on every build and (worse)
# risk being baked into a layer. Two reasons it matters:
#
#   1. Speed — the context is tarred and shipped to the daemon before the build
#      even starts. `.venv` alone is 5.3 GB.
#   2. Safety — `COPY . .` copies whatever is in context. `.env` holds the
#      DeepSeek key, and a key copied into a layer is extractable by anyone who
#      pulls the image, forever, even if a later layer deletes it (layers are
#      append-only). Keys are injected at RUN time as env vars instead — see
#      docker-compose.yml.

# --- Secrets: never, under any circumstances, in an image layer ---
.env

# --- The host venv: 5.3 GB of CUDA torch, and built against the HOST's python ---
# The image builds its own CPU-only venv from uv.lock. Copying this one in would
# be both enormous and broken.
.venv/

# --- Corpus / index / model caches: mounted as volumes at runtime, not baked ---
data/

# --- VCS + local tooling ---
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# --- Python noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Not needed to SERVE: exploration, eval harness, docs, personal brief ---
notebooks/
eval/
docs/
CLAUDE.md

# --- The build's own recipes ---
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
